<title>INDIA: Chowdhry elected Delhi bourse president.</title>
<headline>Chowdhry elected Delhi bourse president.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Delhi Stock Exchange (DSE) said on Monday its board of directors had appointed Deepak Chowdhry as the president of the stock exchange.</p>
<p>The board, including representatives of the Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI), unanimously elected Choudhry in place of Paramjit Singh, who has been suspended from the board, DSE officials said.</p>
<p>Singh was suspended earlier this month after alleged irregularities in his broking firm, Paramjit Singh and Company.</p>
<p>Chowdhry's tenure is scheduled to end in September this year.</p>
</text>
